# Quarantined flaky steps. Read by scripts/run-test-list.mjs.
# Format: <step> | <case prefix> [| <case prefix> ...]
# A case prefix is the start of the FAIL message (the text after "FAIL: ") of an assertion known to flake. A listed
# step that fails is retried ONCE only when every FAIL line it printed starts with one of its case prefixes; a
# failure anywhere else in the file, a crash that prints no FAIL line, or a timeout is a real failure, never retried.
# A pass on the retry is reported in its own "quarantined flaky steps" section and does not turn the gate red; a
# second failure is a real failure. A step here must also be on a gate list (test-list-completeness checks it).
# Add a step only with the evidence that it flakes on an unchanged tree, and name the flaking case(s).
#
# voice.button: the timing-sensitive mic status restore (frontend/app/voice.js) loses a race under load; the
# assertions seen failing (memory voice-button-test-is-flaky, 2026-07-31, 1 in 6 standalone runs and 2 of 4 gates,
# trunk too) are the stt 403 / stt degrade status reads and the transcript send.
test/voice.button.test.js | stt 403: | stt degrade: | a successful listen still sends the transcript
# save-quota-writethrough: case Q3 (queued acknowledgement) races CloudSave's debounced writes against the test's
# tick under load, on trunk too, and reruns alone green. Its precondition failing fails the rest of Q3 with it.
test/save-quota-writethrough.test.js | Q3
